    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0960" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2386: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-07T11:00:00+01:00">November 7,
                            1935—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 7—6:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. Letter signed by Vasconcellos, President of Committee of Coordination,
                    addressed to me dated November 6, reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to transmit to you herewith, in accordance with the
                            decision of the Coordination Committee, the resolutions and decisions
                            adopted at the close of its second session on November 2,<anchor n="68"
                                xml:id="d731-f1"/> the minutes of that meeting,<anchor n="69"
                                xml:id="d731-f2"/> and the replies of governments to the five
                            proposals adopted during the first session.<anchor n="69"
                                xml:id="d731-f3"/> I would be grateful if you would be good enough
                            to transmit this documentation to the Secretary of State in
                            Washington.</p>
                        <p>I need not add that I continue to be at the disposal of the United States
                            Government, in accordance with my letter of October 21, addressed to the
                            Secretary of State.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Coordinate letter and enclosures being forwarded by mail steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Berengaria</hi> sailing 13th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
